BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c50cb22b-6768-408b-939b-143b03b24487@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T153300
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T170000
SUMMARY:Sun Rose
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Since starting the Sun Rose project in 2022\, Samu has been ded
 icated to bringing ecstatic ritual to the dancefloor and celebrating resil
 ience\, community\, and collaboration on the decks. He has performed at En
 vision\, Dance Church\, Nectar\, Soar\, LIB\, the Castle in France\, Ohm i
 n Berlin and the Soundgarden and Abraxas at Burning Man along with countle
 ss house parties and ecstatic dances around the globe.\n\nInstagram: https
 ://www.instagram.com/Samusunrose\nSoundCloud: http://soundcloud.com/djsunr
 ose/rythmeduchataeu\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/sun
 -rose-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ec0807e1-9b14-4e66-96c5-6822ae08e930@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T183000
SUMMARY:Lili Rose
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:LiLi Rose is a DJ from the West Kootenay Region\, BC who plays 
 mainly global influenced electronic dance music. “I love electronic musi
 c with global rhythms and traditional instruments\, but I also love music 
 from the ghettos and underground scenes from around the world. I play genr
 es like Batida\, new cumbia\, folktronica\, Latin club\, baile funk\, amap
 iano\, Afro house\, UK funky and more!”\n\nShe is a connoisseur  of sou
 nd and loves to dance. She has played many stages such as global heat\, Sh
 ambhala music festival and DJs ecstatic dance events across British Columb
 ia. Her collection of music is always growing\, and her style is continual
 ly evolving as she searches out the freshest sounds from around the world.
 \n\nSoundCloud: http://soundcloud.com/lili-rose-23\nInstagram: http://inst
 agram.com/lilis_creations_art/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/p
 roducts/lili-rose
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9112ec55-8466-4548-83aa-593c4a4c4d24@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
SUMMARY:Sijay James
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Sijay James has been DJ’ing since 1996 when he caught the vin
 yl bug in the earlier days of the Vancouver electronic dance music scene. 
 He has performed at venues around the world and has been a strong part of 
 the west coast festival community for nearly 3 decades. A resident of Nels
 on BC since 2008\, Sijay has also been a creative force in the graphic des
 ign and art direction of numerous festivals\, including a tenure as art di
 rector for Shambhala\, playing a large role in the development of Dance Mu
 sic culture behind the scenes.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/onbey
 ond23\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/onbeyond/\n\nProfile: https://
 thenectarfestival.com/products/sijay-james
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d7dff57e-4273-40ac-8400-0b9fc1fa08f3@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
SUMMARY:Applecat
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:AppleCat is an internationally acclaimed DJ\, producer\, and vo
 calist from Canada’s West Coast\, known for blending Deep Dubstep\, Fair
 ytale Bass\, Trap\, and various world influences into cinematic\, grimy pe
 rformances. Her sets feel less like a DJ set and more like a spell: bass-d
 riven\, emotional\, and rooted in the belief that “a revolution without 
 dancing is not a revolution worth having.”\n\nOnstage\, she fuses live m
 ashups\, reworks\, and ethereal vocals into hypnotic basslines that move a
 udiences both physically and emotionally. This dark booty bouncing dubwitc
 h bends the perception of "genre" exemplifying her unparalleled "je ne sai
 s quoi.”\n\nShe has performed across North America\, the UK\, and beyond
 \, including Burning Man\, Enchanted Forest Gathering\, Rifflandia\, Futur
 e Forest\, Evolve\, Envision\, and Tall Tree\, sharing lineups with CloZee
 \, Truth\, Emancipator\, Tipper\, The Polish Ambassador\, and The Halluci 
 Nation.\n\nFeatured in the global documentary Amplify Her (2017) and inter
 viewed in DJ Mag\, AppleCat continues to evolve as a primal storyteller an
 d sonic architect.\n\n"Music is a possession that I desire no exorcism fro
 m. " - AppleCat\n\nLinktree: https://linktr.ee/AppleCat\nInstagram: https:
 //www.instagram.com/applecatmusic\nFacebook: http://facebook.com/djappleca
 t\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/applecat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:c06a25f5-efdf-4647-a21d-d9eb8e23aa5a@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T230000
SUMMARY:Kaya Ko
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Kaya Ko is a queer Filipinx vocalist & multi-media artist born 
 on Turtle Island. Their musical style blends between alt-folk\, neo-RnB/So
 ul to HipHop with elements of West-coast Bass and EDM. A mix of classical 
 training\, 12 years of street performance\, 20+ years of stage performance
 s and self-teaching gives Kaya's music an undeniable sense of fluency and 
 experience.\n\nA gifted songwriter since age 10\, violinist since age 5\, 
 Kaya graduated at SAE Institute\, completing their studies as an Electroni
 c Music Producer and Audio Engineer.  Bringing soulful vocals and a rap s
 tyle that is reminiscent of influences such as Lauryn Hill\, Kaya shows ve
 rsatility and style in all of their skills.\n\nA passionate member of the 
 Filipinx Community\, Kaya has roots in the street community as well as oth
 er marginalized groups of people in the diaspora and is a dedicated advoca
 te for voices of radicalized\, oppressed and overlooked Peoples. Seeking t
 o walk as a bridge between worlds\, Kaya hopes to bring people together an
 d Unify Nations with their music.\n\nBorn to entertain with an introspecti
 ve side\, this artist is deeply rooted and offers a wide spectrum of moods
 \, frequencies and flavours to the audience. From stripped down acoustic a
 nd live looping to classic hiphop & rnb performance\, Kaya has a set for a
 nything.\n\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@kaya.ko_music\nInstagram: ht
 tps://www.instagram.com/kaya.ko.music/\nTikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@ka
 ya.ko.music\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/2QZO5j7QLZMYVbyUeQhT
 DL?si=_8UKttl5SiGGwbxQr-OKOQ\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/pro
 ducts/kaya-ko
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d3750cb8-ced4-476a-8cb8-2c9fe7a3fb99@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T230000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T003000
SUMMARY:Casey Club
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Casey Club is carving out his own lane in the global bass music
  scene. Drawing from a deep understanding of garage\, dubstep\, UK bass\, 
 and drum & bass\, he delivers a sound that is unmistakably his own. His ha
 llmark sets are packed with unreleased material\, consistently leaving cro
 wds asking for IDs.\n\nIn 2025\, Casey Club became a mainstay in the Beatp
 ort Dubstep Top 5\, finishing the year as the 4th best-selling artist on t
 he platform. His releases amassed millions of streams and earned global su
 pport from artists spanning scenes and genres\, including Skrillex\, GRiZ\
 , Subtronics\, Four Tet\, Fred again..\, and Chase & Status. His music has
  featured across institutions such as Deadbeats\, UKF\, BBC Radio 1\, Rins
 e FM\, and SWU FM.\n\nLive performances have seen a parallel rise. Highlig
 hts from 2025 include a standout\n\nShambhala debut - drawing shoulder-to-
 shoulder crowds at 2pm on Thursday - followed by a sold-out run of Canadi
 an headline shows. In the UK\, he appeared at major festivals including B
 oomtown and Love Saves The Day.\n\n2026 will mark another major step forwa
 rd\, with Casey Club set to embark on his debut US and North American tour
 \, flowing directly into a packed Australian tour\, alongside further inte
 rnational dates planned throughout the year. If you don’t know about Cas
 ey Club yet\, the time to play catch up as he continues to break down ever
 y barrier put in front of him.\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/cas
 eyclubofficial/\nTikTok: https://www.tiktok.com/@caseyclubofficial\nSpotif
 y: https://open.spotify.com/artist/2bmnpyZiHHOCrU988FwaJj?si=JKrmYbBIRaKoH
 YMIaMCRYw\nApple Music: https://music.apple.com/ca/artist/casey-club/17325
 26802\nWebsite: https://music.amazon.com/artists/B0CW6NRZBZ/casey-club?mar
 ketplaceId=ATVPDKIKX0DER&musicTerritory=US&ref=dm_sh_6laJXCqrajzMvuQbHq8QJ
 P1dZ\nWebsite: https://www.beatport.com/artist/casey-club/1189100\n\nProfi
 le: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/casey-club-and-snuffy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cbf6202e-4d38-4c80-ab00-8bb556024e59@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T003000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T020000
SUMMARY:Snuffy
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Snuffy is the solo project of an innovative DJ and producer who
  has made a significant impact on the electronic music scene with his dyna
 mic sound\, rooted in 140 BPM and breaks. Fusing heavy basslines with vibr
 ant\, dancefloor-ready energy\, his music bridges the underground and main
 stream with a unique blend of grit and groove. Drawing influence from trai
 lblazers like Bakey\, Visages\, and Skream\, Snuffy crafts tracks that res
 onate with both the heady atmospherics and high-energy moments that define
  modern bass music.\n\nSince making his mark with releases on labels like 
 Memory Palace\, Subsidia\, Odyzey\, Qualia\, and Bite This\, Snuffy has es
 tablished himself as a forward-thinking artist with a talent for pushing b
 oundaries. His collaborations with notable producers like EAZYBAKED\, Play
 erDave\, JordnMoody\, Snowy\, and countless others further showcase his ab
 ility to blend his sound with a diverse range of styles\, creating fresh a
 nd exciting music that continues to captivate global audiences.\n\nWith a 
 rising presence on the U.S. festival circuit\, Snuffy’s electrifying liv
 e performances further solidify his reputation\, creating a visceral conne
 ction with fans and making him a staple in the festival scene. As he conti
 nues to evolve\, Snuffy is dedicated to pushing the limits of bass-driven 
 electronic music while keeping his roots firmly connected to the dancefloo
 r.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/snuffysounds\nSpotify: https://op
 en.spotify.com/artist/08yNyQvMaC3dLtOthzhPaZ?si=0oibTMvlRy-fLt_jFjB3yQ\nIn
 stagram: https://www.instagram.com/snuffy.bass?utm_source=ig_web_button_sh
 are_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/
 products/snuffy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6e85259d-20af-495b-b82a-037947adb015@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T020000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T033000
SUMMARY:Entelechy
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Active in the West Coast electronic music scene for over two de
 cades\, Entelechy helped found ‘Returning Saturn’ events and artist co
 llective\, and ‘Ironic Spin’ sound camp. Versed across many genres and
  settings\, from intimate living room gatherings to large multi-day festiv
 als\, Entelechy plays for both dancers and listeners. Weaving a background
  of music theory\, composition\, arrangement\, and production\, with novel
  exploration of emerging styles\, frequencies\, and harmonies\; creating s
 tories of becoming through countless sets across the West Coast and beyond
 . The term "Entelechy" describes the force within and around us that guide
 s us to realize our inborn nature and manifest our highest potential in th
 is life.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/entelechy\nInstagram: https
 ://www.instagram.com/dj_entelechy/\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/ret
 urning-saturn\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/entelechy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b64bcd42-b696-455b-b8ee-f180c412c916@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T033000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T050000
SUMMARY:Dwam
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:DWAM blends dubstep\, UKG\, bass\, and club music into high-ene
 rgy sets full of rolling grooves\, heavy low end\, and curveball selection
 s that keep the dancefloor moving. Built for big systems and late nights.\
 n\nBehind the scenes\, he has co-founded Victoria's Mind Garden helping pr
 omote shows with a focus on high level production and intentional spaces t
 o create a community of open artistic expression.\n\nLinktree: http://link
 tr.ee/dwambeats\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/dwam.beats\nSpotify:
  https://open.spotify.com/artist/4Tnfi7lPUtnTXd50SKsy4A?si=i8_H_Dp8SU-QbFA
 VNRisNQ\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/dwam
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0c0ee29f-16dc-447c-99be-2e3f8c7411de@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T153300
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T170000
SUMMARY:The Moon Bodega
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:“Delicately engineered to activate the lightness and darkness
  in the muladhara\, bless your wounds\; that’s how the light gets in.
 ”\n\nZain Burgess\, aka Moon Bodega\, has been DJ’ing for two decades.
  He saved up his earnings from A&W at that tender age of 16 to afford a m
 ixer and two turntables. He's been obsessed and involved in rave culture e
 ver since.\n\nHe's relentlessly curious about up-and-coming sounds from di
 fferent areas of the world and combining them with samples and sounds fro
 m the past. He will take you into the depths of your body and drive you in
 to a hypnotic\, somatic exploration of your body. Now combining his love o
 f somatic therapy\, he infuses the two to help move stuck emotions on the 
 dance-floor. Energy transmutation. The epic flight of sonic  storytelling
 . He created and is running a monthly series in Victoria for psychedelic a
 nd hypnotic electronic music\, called Space Temple.\n\nWhen Zain is not in
 volved in music he works in film production. Cinema is clearly a huge infl
 uence in his work.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/zain-burgess\n\nP
 rofile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/moon-bodega
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7f5c7204-3c13-41ad-8fd2-3cefe3293a6d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T183000
SUMMARY:Khan
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Khan is a seasoned DJ with decades of experience behind the dec
 ks\, known for his unique sonic identity that seamlessly blends Middle Eas
 tern melodies with a diverse spectrum of House and Bass genres. From the p
 ulsating depths of Deep Dubstep to the infectious grooves of Trance\, Prog
 ressive\, Funky\, Deep\, and Bass House\, his sets are a testament to his 
 wide-ranging musical expertise.\n\nWhat truly sets Khan apart is the intri
 cate infusion of organic Middle Eastern elements\, juxtaposed with the raw
  machine energy of electronic music. This energetic contrast spins a capti
 vating sound narrative\, moving from profound soulfulness to grooves that 
 compel dancers to surrender entirely to the rhythm.\n\nInspired by boundar
 y-pushing artists like Sasha\, John Digweed\, and Widdler\, Khan has grace
 d popular events such as Shambhala\, Electric Love\, Bass Coast and Astral
  harvest. He's held residencies with collectives like Beheshto Productions
 \, Area709 and presently Ironic Spin\, showcasing his ability to ignite da
 nce floors with diverse and captivating soundscapes.\n\nWith a musical jou
 rney woven with cultural threads\, Khan invites listeners to lose themselv
 es in an immersive auditory experience where the organic and the electroni
 c dance in harmony. His performances have earned him recognition and prais
 e from fans and industry peers alike.\n\nFacebook:\n\nSoundCloud:\n\nFaceb
 ook: https://www.facebook.com/khansmixes\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.c
 om/khan\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/khan
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:06277fc9-b84f-441d-a374-5a75dd1997f0@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T200000
SUMMARY:Rah
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:RAH aka Noradawn\, has a nomadic spirit\, having lived many pla
 ces in her life. She was born in Alberta and spent part of her childhood i
 n Florida and Colombia\, South America. She currently lives in a forest on
  the edge of the South Okanagan Valley and spends time between her home th
 ere and the west coast. As the founder and director of Revel\, a family-fr
 iendly dance music festival rooted in sound system and rave culture — sh
 e believes the dancefloor is a place of communion and healing.\n\nShe has 
 been a DJ for around 27 years — first touching the decks in 1999 and pla
 ying out for the first time in 2000. With a focus on DnB and Jungle\, she 
 loves to weave the many musical influences that have shaped her throughout
  her sets. Her sound ranges from heavy\, deep and electric to ethereal\, s
 oulful and syncopated — with minimal stripped breaks to cascading rhythm
 s occasionally layered with melody and vocals. With a classical piano upbr
 inging and a lifetime of immersion across genres\, her musical knowledge r
 uns deep\, and with it she weaves these various threads of sound into a ne
 w story.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/rahrhythms/rahrevel2516bit\
 nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/noradawntribe/\nFacebook: https://ww
 w.facebook.com/nora.dawn.9/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/prod
 ucts/rah
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:493e7e5e-0609-4f97-aca9-4232907af799@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
SUMMARY:Aninja
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Ryan Halston AKA ANiNjA is a Drum and Bass Producer/DJ from Van
 couver\, Canada. His style focuses on blending deep minimal rollers with a
  healthy selection of MCs and vocalists. With over 20 years of making musi
 c under his belt\, his sound selection is sure to get the attention of a c
 rowd. Ryan began DJing in 2013\, originally as a Hip Hop DJ/producer/MC kn
 own as SkyWryter hosting local shows in the Okanagan. He eventually found 
 a love for funky glitch hop and began playing more electronic shows. After
  his first summer playing raves he decided it was time to separate his ele
 ctronic DJing from his Hip Hop persona. Ryan's first official show as ANiN
 jA was in 2018. In 2020 his style shifted to Drum and Bass and he began a 
 process of rebuilding his studio\, followed by a move to Vancouver in 2021
  where he has been active in the underground scene. Fast forward to 2026\,
  many of ANiNjA's sets are packed full of his original music as well as ex
 clusive tracks and dubs from some of his favorite artists with the goal of
  bringing the underground UK DnB sounds to Canada. Among all his musical p
 ursuits he has also been a sound engineer since 2012 who has worked many o
 f the best venues and festivals in BC. Currently the primary sound tech at
  Red Room Vancouver for Subculture Saturdays\, it's safe to say he has a f
 inger on the pulse of the underground electronic music scene.\n\nSoundClou
 d: https://soundcloud.com/aninjamusic\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.co
 m/aninja_dj\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@aninja_dj\n\nProfile: https
 ://thenectarfestival.com/products/aninja
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ae687f55-2435-4978-9f03-610be5befbf4@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T223000
SUMMARY:Kytami x Gospel of Her
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:There are few acts on the west coast combining live instrumenta
 tion\, high energy and gritty bass music with the ferocity and craft than 
 violinist Kytami. She has made it her mission to create a truly unique sou
 nd that would be instantly recognizable as her own all the while drawing o
 n her love of Drum n Bass\, Hip Hop\, Punk and bass heavy dance music. Sin
 ce the release of her eponymous award winning album in 2013 she has solidi
 fied her presence in Canada's DnB scene\, standing out in an already satur
 ated musical landscape. Alongside her long time collaborator Phonik Ops\, 
 she has co-produced exclusive guest mixes for the DnB Show on BBC Radio 1 
 and BeatLab Radio and continuously built up her fan base with spectacular 
 live shows and an ever-increasing catalogue of impactful music.\n\nGospel 
 of HER is an emerging DJ from Victoria\, B.C. Primarily focusing on Drum a
 nd Bass\, her deep\, yet energetic sound has been gaining recognition loc
 ally and worldwide online. Her performances center around building deep co
 nnection and her style blends atmospheric textures\, dark rollers\, and he
 avy bass lines. During her performance you will ride the emotional intensi
 ty into a powerful late night journey.\n\n=========================\n\nWeb
 site: https://www.kytami.com/\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/0L
 V73kKoy3jOem7j7HvzJt\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/TheKytami\nSoundClo
 ud: https://soundcloud.com/kytami\nInstagram: https://instagram.com/kytami
 \nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/Kytami/\nWebsite: https://www.twitch.
 tv/kytamimusic\nSoundCloud: https://on.soundcloud.com/rVx1uREHtcVOLmCFrs\n
 Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/gospelofher?utm_source=ig_web_button_
 share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/gosp
 elofher\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/kytami
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:741c65c4-35b3-4b9b-b178-b78ac7ffc078@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T223000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T000000
SUMMARY:Mirage
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Mirage's musical journey mirrors the illusory nature of sound\,
  bending and refracting across genres\, creating an experience that captiv
 ates and transcends expectations in the realm of music production. Mirage 
 immerses himself in the depths of 140\, Breaks\, Jungle & Drum & Bass\, co
 nsistently pushing the boundaries.\n\nBeyond the studio\, Mirage is a comm
 unity-builder in Victoria\, B.C.'s music scene. The architect behind Dubve
 rsified Culture\, he founded this underground community in 2017 with a mis
 sion to elevate local West Coast bass artists and forge connections across
  global Bass music and the local dance music scenes. Host of a monthly sho
 w on Subtle Radio (UK)\, Mirage's dedication underscores his commitment to
  navigating the ever-evolving landscape of electronic music.\n\nSoundCloud
 : https://soundcloud.com/miragemusique\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.c
 om/miragemusique/\nYouTube: https://www.youtube.com/@Miragemusique\n\nProf
 ile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/mirage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf51e41b-2d69-4b54-97f1-d7e0394ea39c@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T013000
SUMMARY:Mazeguider
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:The Mazeguider brings a singular sensibility to the decks\, wea
 ving journeys full of emotional power\, compelling sounds\, and undeniable
  grooves. The genre may mutate as the freshness and novelty shift through 
 different sounds and styles\, but it's all driven by a call\, a beacon pul
 sing that beckons us forward on each step of the journey home.\n\nAn OG of
  West Coast festival culture\, the Mazeguider returns to the decks after r
 ocking countless dancefloors over his career. He is the producer and creat
 ive director of Nectar Festival\, a new Summer Solstice festival in the be
 autiful Gulf Islands of BC. He was one of the co-founders of the legendary
  Tribal Harmonix collective and long-running Intention Gathering. His TEDx
  talk on "Transformational festivals" in 2010 led to The Bloom documentary
  series that filmed 24 festivals worldwide and screened in over 80 locatio
 ns globally.\n\nListen to new mix (Ethnic Midtempo / Organic House) out no
 w!\n\nFacebook:\n\nSoundCloud:\n\nBloom Series:\n\nSoundCloud: https://sou
 ndcloud.com/mazeguider/the-immaculate-day\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.
 com/p/Mazeguider-100064063570940\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/mazeg
 uider\nWebsite: https://thebloom.tv/watch/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfe
 stival.com/products/mazeguider
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4ec55e4a-d161-44d7-a3de-395bfe08d4d3@nectar2026
