BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cf6f7329-aaf3-43cf-8b51-c9df5c90e818@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T003000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T013000
SUMMARY:Abstrakt Sonance & The Nectar Orchestra
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Something truly special is being created for Nectar 2026. This 
 year we are honoured to premiere the live immersive multimedia debut of Ab
 strakt Sonance & The Nectar Orchestra\, featuring Kytami\, Sosita\, Rob Ch
 ristian\, Marshall Rasmussen\, Lady of the Mist\, Dredekop\, Doug Gorkoff\
 , Liesl Petersen\, and Tomemos.\n\nGuided by one of our region's brightest
  musical visionaries\, Abstrakt Sonance serves as conductor — crafting a
 n expansive yet intimate performance brought to life with live instrumenta
 tion and vocals\, custom visuals\, and ceremonial choreography to uplift o
 ur spirits at this critical time on the planet. Together these elements we
 ave a powerful journey of transformation\, resilience\, and renewal.\n\nJo
 in us at Nectar Festival to witness this singular moment as it comes alive
 .\n\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/00qKBesewdWy5l0bpMdosp?si=c6
 9_fb0hSbqKQn2pr5Pbwg\nSoundCloud: http://www.soundcloud.com/abstraktsonanc
 e\nWebsite: https://abstraktsonance.ca\nInstagram: http://www.instagram.co
 m/abstraktsonance\nFacebook: http://www.facebook.com/abstraktsonance\nWebs
 ite: https://www.kytami.com/\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/kytami\nI
 nstagram: https://instagram.com/kytami\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.c
 om/sositaart/\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/marshall.rasmussen/\nS
 potify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/75XUnXCiMd1YMHwBvAIfnn?si=nWkSdA8R
 QYaepKzqzcEm6A\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/robnchrisca?utm_sourc
 e=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxNw==\nSpotify: https://open.s
 potify.com/artist/5GmTnqtSTio7KExuVLfw4W?si=HuX4fHcNQxmQgXfLvSGajw\n\nProf
 ile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/abstrakt-sonance-the-nectar-or
 chestra
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7bb8e726-6ac9-4318-bec5-7e53ff286f71@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T013000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T030000
SUMMARY:Saturna
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Originating from the Sunshine Coast\, British Columbia\, ethere
 al beatsmith Saturna has an artistic voice unlike any other. By drawing in
 spiration from a plethora of sources\, Saturna has crafted a stirring and 
 enigmatic production style that blends meticulously carved soundscapes wit
 h irresistible grooves. Saturna is a sonic story-teller who weaves layers 
 of deeply emotive melodies and organic rhythms with cinematic flair.\n\nBy
  tapping into the deeper realms of organic bass\, Saturna strives to lead 
 his listeners into bold and perplexing new frontiers. As a lifelong musici
 an\, the Canadian producer is dedicated to stitching together narrative th
 reads into a tapestry of distorted synths\, warm throbbing basslines and l
 ush percussive elements. Smooth\, sonorous\, and cleansing\, Saturna’s s
 ounds oscillate between dreamy ballads and kaleidoscopic voyages.\n\nConne
 ction is the focus of Saturna’s live performances. By incorporating emot
 ional touchstones in his music\, Saturna develops strong connective bonds 
 with his listener. His unique style evokes a sense of looking inward to fi
 nd the limitless expanse within us all. As the founder of Wildlife Divisio
 n\, Saturna is leading a collective of daring artists focused on pushing t
 he boundaries through sound experimentation and live curation.\n\nSaturna 
 has amassed an impressive collection of transcendent releases\, including 
 his critically acclaimed\, Departure EP\, which was released earlier this 
 year. With a slew of new projects forthcoming on his imprint Wildlife Divi
 sion as well as a slate of live shows and festivals booked throughout Nort
 h America\, Saturna is primed to establish himself as a force in the elect
 ronic music landscape.\n\nSpotify: https://open.spotify.com/artist/6Y3GYer
 mT3jkAuq3A5vLXn?si=iaTUZ2R-QdemoXdHDk5GFA\nInstagram: https://www.instagra
 m.com/saturnasound?utm_source=ig_web_button_share_sheet&igsh=ZDNlZDc0MzIxN
 w==\nSoundCloud: https://on.soundcloud.com/vW5bhU5wX2CKSEkTGd\nBandcamp: h
 ttps://saturnasound.bandcamp.com/album/departure\nWebsite: https://saturna
 .komi.io\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/saturna
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b891dc5a-25fc-4a81-9118-5ec5a1ec8f41@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T030000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T050000
SUMMARY:Leland River
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:A North-Westcoast fixture - Leland River is a DJ/Producer whose
  growth as an artist and human being is deeply tied to the mycelial webs o
 f the BC festival scene.   Trusted by many of his peers and listeners 
 for his diverse array of productions\, mixes\, and adept sense for playing
  the right music at the right time\; Leland River has been given the contr
 ols at Bass Coast\, Envision\, and Shambhala for 10 years in a row.   
  From a love of hypnotizing rhythms and the low-end of dubstep\, garage\, 
 grime\, breaks\, dancehall\, jungle and techno\; mixed with a disposition 
 for emotive ambience and a love for R&B - Leland River’s music and DJ se
 ts fit better inside a vast large venn diagram than a box.\n\nInstagram:\n
 \nFacebook:\n\nSoundCloud:\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/leland_
 river/\nFacebook: https://www.facebook.com/lelandriver.music/\nSoundCloud:
  https://soundcloud.com/leland_river\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival
 .com/products/leland-river
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:b2c75c0e-5805-4b31-b4e4-510d9ec8449b@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T050000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T063000
SUMMARY:Melo.Nade
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Navin ‘Melo.Nade’ Huq was born and raised in Calgary\, Cana
 da. Growing up with hip-hop culturists\, he learned the art of digging at 
 an early age\, which resulted in an insatiable addiction for finding those
  hard to find gems. As a child\, he would spend time recording mix tapes (
 yes\, cassettes) off the radio\, TV\, and his dad’s records\; satisfying
  his instinctive nature to sequence tracks as well as delve into music tec
 hnology. Navin acquired his first set of turntables in 2003\, and that’s
  when Melo.Nade was born. Originally on the hip-hop tip\, he experimented 
 with mash ups and tempo changes before the age of Serato and digital DJ’
 ing. Countless hours were spent in the progression of turntablism and fusi
 ng the worlds of trip hop\, hip-hop\, funk and breaks\, into an eclectic v
 ibe.\n\nMore recently\, the Melo.Nade sound has evolved to embody the term
  Heavy Chill - downbeat\, yet heavy hitting (from deep dubstep to lustful 
 world beats to breaks\, hip-hop\, and R&B). His endeavours in music produc
 tion are sculpting a fresh sound that fuses classical and worldly instrume
 nts with electronic bass music. The basis of the vibe is flowing and non-r
 epetitive.\n\nIn every set\, he strives to take you on a walk through musi
 c\; not just with his tight mixing\, but also by seamlessly incorporating 
 edits and layers of purposeful cuts/effects and lush melodies. Melo.Nade
 ’s imaginative and intelligent persona is expressed through his music by
  delivering bass-driven grooves while maintaining the melodious merit that
 ’s often lost in electronic translation. His diverse experience gives hi
 m the edge to read crowds and adapt. No set is the same as he stays true t
 o the musical art form of DJ’ing.\n\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/
 melo-nade\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/nav_melo\nFacebook: https:
 //www.facebook.com/Melo.Nade.Sound/\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.
 com/products/melo-nade
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:3274405d-cf98-4a5f-ac2a-7af7465b0112@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T063000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260622T080800
SUMMARY:Okiro
LOCATION:Solstice Stage
DESCRIPTION:Growing up on the West Coast of Canada\, Okiro was shaped by BC
 ’s thriving festival culture\, which sparked his passion for music from 
 an early age. Blending sub-heavy dubstep\, garage\, grime\, rap\, and R&B\
 , Okiro’s sound is both an ode to the UK’s underground bass scene and 
 a reflection of the more melodic influences of the West Coast. With a keen
  ear for music and an instinct for the right sound at the right moment\, h
 is sets move fluidly across BPMs and styles—always grounded in emotion\,
  depth\, and sonic richness. Even in high-energy moments\, his selections 
 carry a softer\, more melodic touch\, giving his sets a unique ebb and flo
 w. With performances at world-renowned festivals like Shambhala & Bass Coa
 st\, alongside countless local and international shows\, Okiro has built a
  reputation for curating unforgettable experiences. Whether in an intimate
  club or on a festival stage\, his selections create moments that resonate
  far beyond the dancefloor.\n\nInstagram:\n\nFacebook:\n\nSoundCloud:\n\nb
 andcamp:\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/__okiro__\nFacebook: http
 s://www.facebook.com/okirosound\nSoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/okiros
 ound\nBandcamp: https://okiro.bandcamp.com\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfe
 stival.com/products/okiro
END:VEVENT
